> [2e9cf9d](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36002/changes/2e9cf9d7eba20bb2d431ec13a69ce65a163390c9) _txindex: return pruned block hashes from FindTx_:

This can be a bit shorter if we construct the transaction from the file and check its hash inside the `try` block. That also keeps `tx` local and makes the `continue` unnecessary.

Whether a read failure should just log a warning and try the next candidate is a separate question. That behavior predates this PR, and this suggestion leaves it unchanged.

